# agent worktrees — separate git repos, never part of this one
.claude/worktrees/

# Work in progress. `notes` is a symlink to a separate *private* repo
# (kreativitea/articles.omoto.dev) checked out at ~/Code/personal/articles.omoto.dev,
# so drafts are versioned and backed up without ever entering this public one.
#
# Deliberately outside src/, because anything under src/ is Eleventy input and
# would deploy. Publishing moves a piece across the repo boundary — see bin/publish.
#
# No trailing slash, and that is load-bearing: `notes/` matches directories only,
# and git records a symlink as a blob, not a directory. With the slash this
# pattern silently stops matching and the symlink becomes committable.
notes
